# =============================================================================
# Node.js Backend .gitignore
# 
# This file specifies intentionally untracked files for a Node.js/Express.js
# backend project using Node.js v22.x LTS and Express.js v5.1.0
# 
# Purpose: Maintain clean repository, prevent sensitive data exposure,
# and exclude build artifacts and dependencies from version control
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies and Package Management
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Exclude npm-managed dependencies - these are large, auto-generated,
# and should be installed via package.json using npm install
node_modules/

# Package manager lock files (optional exclusion)
# Note: In modern workflows, package-lock.json is often committed
# for reproducible builds, but can be excluded for flexibility
package-lock.json

# Package manager debug and error logs
# Generated during failed installs or runtime errors
npm-debug.log
yarn-debug.log
yarn-error.log

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build Artifacts and Distribution
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Exclude compiled/built output directories
# These are generated from source code and should not be tracked
dist/
build/

# Code coverage reports and test output
# Generated by testing frameworks and coverage tools
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment Configuration and Secrets
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment variable files containing sensitive configuration
# These often contain API keys, database credentials, and other secrets
.env
.env.*

# Local configuration files that may contain sensitive or machine-specific data
*.local

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Development Tool Cache and Temporary Files
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ESLint cache files for improved performance
# Contains processed file information and should be regenerated
.eslintcache

# All log files generated during development and runtime
*.log

# Log directories that may contain application or system logs
logs/

# Temporary directories and files used during development
tmp/
temp/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Process and Runtime Files
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Process ID directories and files
# Used by process managers and should not be committed
pids/
*.pid
*.pid.lock

# Seed files that may contain sensitive database initialization data
*.seed

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Operating System Generated Files
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# macOS Finder metadata files
# Generated automatically by macOS Finder and serve no purpose in repository
.DS_Store

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Security and Compliance Notes
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This .gitignore configuration addresses:
# 
# 1. Version Control Hygiene (Technical Specs 3.6.1):
#    - Excludes auto-generated files (node_modules/, build artifacts)
#    - Prevents large binary files from cluttering repository
#    - Maintains clean, focused codebase with only essential files
#
# 2. Security and Compliance (Technical Specs 2.2.1):
#    - Prevents accidental commit of environment variables (.env files)
#    - Excludes log files that may contain sensitive runtime data
#    - Protects against exposure of process files and temporary data
#
# 3. Build and Dependency Management (Technical Specs 3.6.3):
#    - Excludes node_modules/ as dependencies managed via package.json
#    - Prevents build artifacts from being tracked in source control
#    - Ensures only source code and configuration are version controlled
#
# This configuration supports the Node.js v22.x LTS and Express.js v5.1.0
# technology stack while maintaining enterprise security standards.